  "title": "The seven letter names",
  "summary": "White keys use only seven letters, A to G, and then start again.",
  "minutes": 6,
  "steps": [
    {
      "type": "explain",
      "title": "Only seven letters",
      "body": "The white keys are named with the first seven letters of the alphabet: **A B C D E F G**. After G, the names start again at A.\n\nGoing right (up in pitch), the letters go forward. Going left (down), they go backward.",
      "exampleMidi": [
        60,
        62,
        64,
        65,
        67,
        69,
        71,
        72
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "show",
      "title": "C, D and E",
      "body": "Around each group of two black keys sit C, D and E. D is the white key in the middle of the pair.",
      "highlightMidi": [
        60,
        62,
        64
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "show",
      "title": "F, G, A and B",
      "body": "Around each group of three black keys sit F, G, A and B. Then the next C starts the pattern again.",
      "highlightMidi": [
        65,
        67,
        69,
        71
      ]
    },
